---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="CrashScope 1.1 Released | Marcelo Ellwanger" description="CrashScope 1.1 is a released local-first Windows crash-diagnostics system with 239/239 automated .NET tests, ConfigTrace 1.0.1 provider integration, exact validated release artifacts, upgrade validation and genuine second-PC validation.">
  <section class="case-hero case-hero-featured wrap crashscope-hero">
    <div class="case-title-block">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 · Windows diagnostics · 1.1 released · Systems engineering</p>
      <h1>CrashScope</h1>
      <p class="case-copy">A local-first Windows crash-diagnostics system built to answer a practical question: <em>what happened around the moment my game, GPU driver, AI workload, application or PC failed?</em></p>
      <div class="case-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl/CrashScope/releases/tag/v1.1.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download 1.1.0 ↗</a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl/CrashScope" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View source ↗</a>
        <a class="button" href="#evidence">Validation evidence ↓</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="case-status-panel mono" aria-label="CrashScope release status">
      <div class="case-status-head"><span>PROJECT / STATE</span><b>1.1.0 RELEASED</b></div>
      <div class="case-status-row"><span>Core</span><strong>C# / .NET 10</strong></div>
      <div class="case-status-row"><span>Dashboard</span><strong>React / TypeScript</strong></div>
      <div class="case-status-row"><span>Persistence</span><strong>SQLite</strong></div>
      <div class="case-status-row"><span>Automated tests</span><strong>239/239 PASS</strong></div>
      <div class="case-status-foot"><span class="status-dot">1.1 RELEASED · TWO-PC VALIDATED</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap case-intro-grid">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The problem</p><h2>A crash message is not a diagnosis.</h2></div>
    <div class="case-long-copy">
      <p>I started CrashScope after repeatedly dealing with game, GPU and workload failures where Windows had useful evidence, but it was scattered across hardware state, application events, Windows Error Reporting and reboot history.</p>
      <p>The useful question is rarely “did something crash?” It is “what changed around the incident, what evidence did Windows record, and which conclusions are actually supported?” CrashScope preserves sessions, incidents and nearby evidence without turning correlation into a fake root-cause claim.</p>
      <p>The product is aimed at gamers, PC enthusiasts, hardware testers and local-AI users who want useful diagnostics without another heavyweight monitoring workload or a cloud account in the failure path.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap">
    <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">CrashScope 1.1</p><h2>External evidence without coupling failures together.</h2><p>Version 1.1 adds a generic provider boundary and ships ConfigTrace 1.0.1 as the first process-isolated external evidence source.</p></div>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <article><span class="mono model-index">01</span><h3>Generic EvidenceEvent boundary</h3><p>Provider evidence enters a bounded chronological model with timestamp, source, kind, severity, summary and details. Nearby events are context unless stronger evidence supports a causal claim.</p></article>
      <article><span class="mono model-index">02</span><h3>ConfigTrace 1.0.1</h3><p>The Rust sidecar is off by default, starts only while a selected workload is monitored, and remains process-isolated so provider failure cannot take CrashScope down.</p></article>
      <article><span class="mono model-index">03</span><h3>Privacy-first redaction</h3><p>CrashScope integration uncovered and validated the ConfigTrace 1.0.1 sensitive-key fix for camelCase and PascalCase fields such as apiToken, clientSecret and sessionId.</p></article>
      <article><span class="mono model-index">04</span><h3>Upgrade path proven</h3><p>A true installed 1.0.0 → 1.1.0 upgrade preserved settings, startup state and an existing incident while migrating the settings schema from v2 to v3.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap" id="architecture">
    <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p><h2>One Agent, explicit boundaries, optional sidecars.</h2><p>CrashScope is a modular monolith with explicit boundaries between domain logic, Windows/hardware adapters, runtime orchestration, persistence, the local dashboard and optional external evidence providers.</p></div>
    <div class="architecture-flow">
      <div class="arch-node arch-input"><span class="mono">CORE</span><strong>CrashScope.Core</strong><small>incidents, telemetry, evidence roles, sessions</small></div><div class="arch-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="arch-node"><span class="mono">ADAPTERS</span><strong>Infrastructure</strong><small>hardware, Event Log, WER, SQLite</small></div><div class="arch-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="arch-node"><span class="mono">HOST</span><strong>CrashScope.Agent</strong><small>sampler, persistence, correlation, local API</small></div><div class="arch-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="arch-node arch-output"><span class="mono">PROVIDERS / UI</span><strong>ConfigTrace + React dashboard</strong><small>optional context evidence + local presentation</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="architecture-note mono"><span>RULE</span><p>The dashboard consumes telemetry already produced by the central Agent. ConfigTrace runs only when enabled for a monitored workload and does not create a second general-purpose monitoring stack.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap">
    <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence philosophy</p><h2>Observation is not causation.</h2></div>
    <div class="failure-grid">
      <article><span class="failure-label mono">BAD DIAGNOSIS</span><h3>“VRAM caused your crash.”</h3><p>A single high metric near a failure is not enough to prove root cause.</p><div class="failure-fix"><span>CRASHSCOPE</span><p>Preserve the observed hardware state and nearby Windows evidence, then keep the conclusion proportional to what the evidence supports.</p></div></article>
      <article><span class="failure-label mono">BAD DIAGNOSIS</span><h3>“The renderer change caused it.”</h3><p>A configuration change occurring before an incident is useful temporal evidence, not automatic causation.</p><div class="failure-fix"><span>CRASHSCOPE</span><p>CrashScope can say “Renderer changed 31.8 seconds before this incident.” It does not automatically say the change caused the incident.</p></div></article>
      <article><span class="failure-label mono">BAD DIAGNOSIS</span><h3>“One Windows event explains everything.”</h3><p>Event Log and WER records can be strong evidence without being a complete explanation.</p><div class="failure-fix"><span>CRASHSCOPE</span><p>Windows evidence is correlated with session, workload and machine context before stronger language is used.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap" id="evidence">
    <div class="field-grid">
      <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Final 1.1 validation</p><h2>Low overhead with the provider off or active.</h2><p>These are measured release-validation results, not universal guarantees for every PC.</p></div>
      <div class="field-console mono">
        <div><span>automated .NET tests</span><b class="accent-value">239/239 PASS</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace OFF · avg Agent CPU</span><b class="accent-value">0.2365%</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace OFF · avg working set</span><b>91.71 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace OFF · peak working set</span><b>94.58 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace OFF · avg private memory</span><b>34.76 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace ON · avg Agent CPU</span><b>0.1966%</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace ON · avg working set</span><b>95.36 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace ON · peak working set</span><b>97.31 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace provider · avg CPU</span><b>0%</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace provider · avg / peak WS</span><b>4.96 / 4.99 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>ConfigTrace provider · avg private</span><b>0.91 MB</b></div>
        <div><span>stale frames / delivery misses</span><b>0 / 0</b></div>
        <div class="field-result"><span>release interpretation</span><strong>PUBLIC 1.1.0</strong></div>
        <div class="field-health"><span>UPGRADE</span><b>PASS</b><span>SECOND PC</span><b>PASS</b><span>PRIVACY</span><b>PASS</b></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="architecture-note mono"><span>HARDWARE SCOPE</span><p>Primary validation passed on Ryzen 5 7500F + Radeon RX 9070 XT. Genuine second-PC automated and manual visual validation also passed on Windows 10 with Intel Core i5-3210M + Intel HD Graphics 4000. NVIDIA GPU hardware remains an unvalidated path and is not presented as tested.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap">
    <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy + security</p><h2>Useful diagnostics without making a cloud account part of the failure path.</h2></div>
    <div class="rules-table">
      <div class="rule-row"><span class="rule-no mono">01</span><strong>Network boundary</strong><p>The API and dashboard are localhost-only rather than exposed as a remote service.</p><b>LOCALHOST</b></div>
      <div class="rule-row"><span class="rule-no mono">02</span><strong>Data handling</strong><p>No analytics or automatic diagnostic upload is required for normal runtime use.</p><b>LOCAL-FIRST</b></div>
      <div class="rule-row"><span class="rule-no mono">03</span><strong>Provider secret handling</strong><p>Final provider-journal validation passed and the plaintext test secret was not found in the journal or CrashScope incident output.</p><b>REDACTED</b></div>
      <div class="rule-row"><span class="rule-no mono">04</span><strong>Failure isolation</strong><p>ConfigTrace runs as a separate process and its lifecycle is bounded to the monitored workload.</p><b>ISOLATED</b></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section wrap">
    <div class="case-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Release engineering</p><h2>The exact validated artifacts are public.</h2><p>CrashScope 1.0.0 and 1.1.0 were published from privacy-safe public source snapshots whose Git trees match the privately validated engineering release boundaries.</p></div>
    <div class="skill-matrix">
      <div><span>1.0 provenance</span><p>Validated private engineering boundary: <code>10c5769364068619f026e609a3c221d2665ede57</code>. Public v1.0.0 snapshot: <code>4336d5cde8b2e0fcd07e3397abe0b72826b6a49f</code>.</p></div>
      <div><span>1.1 provenance</span><p>Validated private engineering boundary: <code>e51943f6b7aecaf98223ef30cbec10ef94c1eba1</code>. Public v1.1.0 snapshot: <code>341487a0f82c15523611a92fb2829a16cf97d2a7</code>.</p></div>
      <div><span>Portable 1.1</span><p><code>CrashScope-v1.1.0-win-x64.zip</code><br/>SHA-256: <code>4ac728d03d634218add25d94e69a1a55ddd3283b6afc786dc155e1e7e15360a9</code></p></div>
      <div><span>Installer 1.1</span><p><code>CrashScope-Setup-1.1.0.exe</code><br/>SHA-256: <code>eb0acdab0f1da5ae5fbaeceadbd3691ee188f0d42204ddffc9527aa38f28062f</code></p></div>
      <div><span>Release pipeline</span><p>The current public release workflow was repaired to acquire and verify ConfigTrace 1.0.1 before portable smoke testing, then passed publicly.</p></div>
      <div><span>Public-history boundary</span><p>The full engineering history remains private because historical commit metadata included personal author/committer email information; the public repository exposes clean source snapshots instead.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section case-closing wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">CrashScope 1.1 · released</p>
    <h2>Validated, downloadable and still designed to stay out of the way.</h2>
    <p>CrashScope 1.1 combines local Windows evidence, persistent incidents and optional ConfigTrace context while preserving the core rule that temporal correlation is not automatically root cause.</p>
    <div class="case-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl/CrashScope/releases/tag/v1.1.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download 1.1.0 ↗</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl/CrashScope" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Source ↗</a>
      <a class="button" href="/">Back to portfolio ↑</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <style>
    @media (max-width:820px) {
      .crashscope-hero {
        gap:27px !important;
        padding-top:40px !important;
        padding-bottom:50px !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-title-block h1 {
        margin-top:13px !important;
        margin-bottom:18px !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-copy {
        font-size:.98rem !important;
        line-height:1.67 !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-actions {
        display:grid !important;
        grid-template-columns:1fr !important;
        gap:8px !important;
        margin-top:22px !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-actions .button {
        min-height:46px !important;
        width:100%;
        justify-content:center;
        font-size:.74rem !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-actions .button.primary {
        min-height:50px !important;
        font-size:.80rem !important;
      }

      .crashscope-hero .case-status-panel {
        padding:14px !important;
        border-radius:10px;
        box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.25),inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.015);
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-head {
        padding-bottom:11px !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-head b {
        width:max-content;
        max-width:100%;
        padding:5px 7px;
        border:1px solid rgba(214,255,87,.20);
        border-radius:5px;
        background:rgba(214,255,87,.025);
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row {
        min-height:45px !important;
        padding:10px 0 !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row span {
        font-size:.55rem !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row strong {
        font-size:.88rem !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-foot {
        padding-top:11px !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-foot .status-dot {
        font-size:.49rem !important;
        line-height:1.42 !important;
      }

      #evidence .field-console {
        box-shadow:0 20px 48px rgba(0,0,0,.20),inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.012);
      }
      #evidence .field-console .accent-value {
        font-size:.84rem;
      }
      #evidence .field-console .field-result {
        background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(214,255,87,.025),transparent 76%);
      }

      .case-closing .case-actions {
        display:grid !important;
        grid-template-columns:1fr !important;
        gap:8px !important;
      }
      .release-pending {
        position:relative;
        min-height:46px !important;
        justify-content:center;
        color:#8b938d !important;
        border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08) !important;
        background:rgba(255,255,255,.006) !important;
        cursor:default;
        pointer-events:none;
      }
      .release-pending::before {
        content:"";
        width:6px;
        height:6px;
        margin-right:8px;
        border-radius:50%;
        background:#79845e;
        box-shadow:0 0 10px rgba(214,255,87,.16);
      }

      /* Status rows enter after the hero copy, making the panel feel intentionally assembled. */
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row,
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-foot {
        animation:crashscope-mobile-row-in .38s cubic-bezier(.22,.75,.24,1) both;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row:nth-child(2) { animation-delay:.14s; }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row:nth-child(3) { animation-delay:.17s; }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row:nth-child(4) { animation-delay:.20s; }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row:nth-child(5) { animation-delay:.23s; }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-foot { animation-delay:.26s; }
      @keyframes crashscope-mobile-row-in {
        from { opacity:0; transform:translateY(5px); }
        to { opacity:1; transform:translateY(0); }
      }
    }

    @media (min-width:430px) and (max-width:820px) {
      .crashscope-hero .case-actions {
        grid-template-columns:1.15fr .85fr !important;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width:370px) {
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row {
        min-height:0 !important;
      }
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-head b {
        width:100%;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce) {
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-row,
      .crashscope-hero .case-status-foot {
        animation:none !important;
        transform:none !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>